# What EAS Build uploads to Expo, and what it does not.
#
# EAS packs the project from the git repository root, and where this file
# exists it is read INSTEAD of .gitignore. So it does two jobs: it keeps
# everything outside mobile/ - Terraform, the Lambdas, docs, anything
# untracked at the root - off Expo's servers, and it repeats every rule in
# .gitignore, which would otherwise stop applying to the upload.
#
# A rule added to .gitignore is added here too.

# Everything but the mobile app. NO TRAILING SLASH on the negation: EAS's
# matcher reads "!/mobile/" as matching nothing and uploads an empty
# archive. "!/mobile" is what `eas build:inspect --stage archive` showed
# working on 7 October.
/*
!/mobile

# --- .gitignore, repeated ---------------------------------------------------

# Terraform
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Variables - may contain secrets
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example

# Credentials
*.pem
*.key
.env

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Build artefacts
build/

memo-result.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pdf

site/dist/
site/node_modules/

/*.txt

# Mobile app (Expo): dependencies and Expo's local cache
mobile/**/node_modules/
mobile/**/.expo/
